  "narrative": "The clinically meaningful threshold is treated as approximately 10% of the absolute overall outcome mean. For outcome_013 this is about 0.0269; for outcome_015 about 0.0250; and for outcome_014 about 0.0093. Estimates are already signed to each claim direction. H79 is the strongest new result: in high measured feature_061 (ge 63), feature_065=1 versus 0 has signed effect +0.1810 [0.0966, 0.2653], with both bounds far above the outcome_013 clinical threshold. This is a meaningful dataset-specific subgroup association, so I accept it and request independent validation because the subgroup is small enough (88 exposed) and post-selected that validation is scientifically useful. H80, the complementary low feature_061 stratum (le 44.75), is positive but imprecise: +0.0567 [-0.0085, 0.1220], so it is unresolved. H81, the formal high feature_061 interaction, is also positive but its lower bound +0.0009 is below the outcome_013 clinical threshold, so effect modification is not clinically established despite supporting high-stratum concentration. For outcome_015, H82 rejects the stronger-dependency claim within high feature_061: signed estimate -0.0211 and upper bound +0.0176, both unfavorable relative to the claimed direction and clinical threshold. H83 shows a borderline positive low feature_061 outcome_015 estimate +0.0421 [0.0004, 0.0838], but the lower bound is below threshold, so it is deferred rather than accepted; I registered a formal low-feature_061 interaction refinement to test whether the feature_065 effect on outcome_015 is genuinely larger in that stratum. The feature_008 tests are not informative enough for clinical conclusions: H70 is near-null but extremely wide, and H90 is small with interval crossing the clinical threshold; both remain unresolved but closed. The broad outcome_013 screens do not identify a new clinically supported predictor: H76 is imprecise below threshold, H77 is rejected because its upper bound is below threshold, and H78